{"causes":["Established by the Congregation for the Doctrine of the Faith in 1992 to provide a comprehensive guide to Catholic doctrine.","Published in response to the need for a clear and concise explanation of Catholic doctrine in the modern era.","Developed in consultation with Catholic theologians and scholars to ensure its accuracy and authority."],"effects":["Provided a clear and concise explanation of Catholic doctrine for Catholics around the world.","Influenced Catholic thought and practice, shaping the way Catholics understand and apply their faith.","Enabled Catholics to better understand and live out their faith in everyday life."],"relationships":[{"sourceSlug":"congregation-for-the-doctrine-of-the-faith","sourceName":"Congregation for the Doctrine of the Faith","verb":"CREATES","targetSlug":"catechism-of-the-catholic-church","targetName":"Catechism of the Catholic Church","context":"The Catechism was created by the Congregation for the Doctrine of the Faith to provide a comprehensive guide to Catholic doctrine."},{"sourceSlug":"pope-john-paul-ii","sourceName":"Pope John Paul II","verb":"INFLUENCES","targetSlug":"catechism-of-the-catholic-church","targetName":"Catechism of the Catholic Church","context":"In 2000, Pope John Paul II recognized the Catechism as a 'document of the universal church'."},{"sourceSlug":"vatican-city","sourceName":"Vatican City","verb":"INFLUENCES","targetSlug":"catechism-of-the-catholic-church","targetName":"Catechism of the Catholic Church","context":"The Catechism is based on the teachings of the Catholic Church, which is headquartered in Vatican City."},{"sourceSlug":"rome","sourceName":"Rome","verb":"INFLUENCES","targetSlug":"catechism-of-the-catholic-church","targetName":"Catechism of the Catholic Church","context":"The Catechism was written in Rome, the seat of the Catholic Church."},{"sourceSlug":"catholic-church","sourceName":"Catholic Church","verb":"INFLUENCES","targetSlug":"catechism-of-the-catholic-church","targetName":"Catechism of the Catholic Church","context":"The Catechism is an official resource of the Catholic Church."},{"sourceSlug":"christianity","sourceName":"Christianity","verb":"INFLUENCES","targetSlug":"catechism-of-the-catholic-church","targetName":"Catechism of the Catholic Church","context":"The Catechism is a resource for Christians of various denominations."},{"sourceSlug":"world","sourceName":"World","verb":"INFLUENCES","targetSlug":"catechism-of-the-catholic-church","targetName":"Catechism of the Catholic Church","context":"The Catechism is a global resource for Catholics around the world."},{"sourceSlug":"20th-century","sourceName":"20th Century","verb":"INFLUENCES","targetSlug":"catechism-of-the-catholic-church","targetName":"Catechism of the Catholic Church","context":"The Catechism was written in the 20th century, a time of significant change and growth for the Catholic Church."}],"places":[{"name":"Vatican City","role":"Headquarters"},{"name":"Rome","role":"Location of publication"},{"name":"Vatican Hill","role":"Location of the Catechism's composition"}],"texts":[{"title":"Wikipedia: Catechism of the Catholic Church","type":"Reference article","slug":"catechism-of-the-catholic-church"}],"externalLinks":["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q75561","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Catechism_of_the_Catholic_Church"],"tags":["literary work","Historical & Literary Texts","cause-and-effect"],"thumbnailUrl":"","quote":"","legacySummary":"Catechism of the Catholic Church contributed to the historical record of the Classical period. Key lasting impacts include: Contributed to cultural heritage and knowledge transmission. Their legacy is studied through the lens of historical causation.","summary":"The Catechism of the Catholic Church (Latin: Catechismus Catholicae Ecclesiae) is the official compendium of Catholic doctrine and teaching, promulgated by Pope John Paul II on 11 October 1992 — the thirtieth anniversary of the opening of the Second Vatican Council — and published in its definitive edition (the editio typica) in Latin in 1997. It is the first universal catechism since the Roman Catechism (Catechismus Romanus) promulgated after the Council of Trent in 1566 — four centuries previously — and reflects the teaching of Vatican II while presenting the whole of Catholic doctrine in a systematic, accessible form intended for the universal Church. Comprising 2,865 numbered paragraphs organized in four 'pillars' (The Creed; The Sacraments; The Commandments; and Prayer), the Catechism covers the entirety of Catholic belief and moral teaching, from the doctrine of the Trinity and Christology through the seven sacraments, through the moral theology of the commandments (including the Church's positions on abortion, contraception, capital punishment, war, social justice, and sexuality), to a systematic treatment of prayer culminating in the Our Father.

The Catechism was initiated at the Extraordinary Synod of Bishops (1985) called to evaluate the reception of Vatican II twenty years after its conclusion, and produced by a commission of twelve cardinals and bishops chaired by Cardinal Joseph Ratzinger (later Pope Benedict XVI) over six years of drafting (1986–1992). Its promulgation under John Paul II — who wrote a special Apostolic Constitution (Fidei Depositum) for its presentation — was a major moment in the pontificate, consolidating the interpretation of Vatican II in a way that both welcomed the Council's renewal and resisted more radical post-conciliar interpretations.

The Catechism has been translated into more than forty languages and has sold tens of millions of copies worldwide — the best-selling catechism in the history of the Catholic Church. Its systematic presentation of Catholic teaching on every aspect of belief, sacramental life, ethics, and prayer makes it the primary reference point for Catholic doctrine for the world's 1.3 billion Catholics and for those seeking to understand Catholic teaching.","subjects":["Catholic Church","Contemporary Era","Theology","Christianity","Religious Texts","Doctrine","20th Century","Vatican"],"frameworks":["RELIGIOUS_INTERPRETATION","STRUCTURAL_ANALYSIS"],"historicalSignificance":{"significanceScore":7,"significanceNarrative":"The Catechism of the Catholic Church has played a significant role in shaping Catholic thought and practice, providing a clear and concise understanding of Catholic doctrine and its application in everyday life.","significanceCategory":"regional"},"_editLog":[]}
